        "original_id": "8611da39-a5fa-50a9-bbff-8940bbb3b44e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Moominpappa at Sea, The Old Man and the Sea, Moominvalley in November\n- People: Ernest Hemingway\n- Topics: literary references, publication dates, series chronology\n\nFacts:\n- Ernest Hemingway wrote The Old Man and the Sea in 1951 in Bimini, Bahamas, and it was published in 1952.\n- Moominpappa at Sea has an original title that loosely references Ernest Hemingway's novel The Old Man and the Sea, but that reference is not preserved in translation.\n- Moominpappa at Sea was published in 1965.\n- Moominvalley in November is set contemporaneously with the 1965 novel Moominpappa at Sea.\n- Moominvalley in November is the only installment in the series in which the Moomin family are absent.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9cf4d5ed-21dc-519b-a7c0-8b1dd4f288ed",
        "text": "Page: Moominpappa at Sea. Sentence: The original title is a loose reference to Hemingway novel \"The Old Man and the Sea\", though this is not reflected in the translation.\nPage: The Old Man and the Sea. Sentence: The Old Man and the Sea is a short novel written by the American author Ernest Hemingway in 1951 in Bimini, Bahamas, and published in 1952.\nPage: Moominvalley in November. Sentence: Set contemporaneously with her previous novel \"Moominpappa at Sea\" (1965), it is the only installment in the series where the titular Moomin family are actually absent.",
